{{Quote|I know the stories. My grandfather worked at an Imperial factory. Put food on the table when he couldn't find work anywhere else. Did that make him evil?|Tamara Ryvora|audio=TamGrandfather-TheNewTrooper.flac|<ref name="The New Trooper" />}}
A [[weapon]]s '''factory''' of the [[Galactic Empire]] operated during the [[Imperial Era]] and employed the eventual [[Tamara Ryvora's grandfather|grandfather]] of the [[human]] [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]]. In [[34 ABY]], Ryvora told the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and the mechanic [[Jarek Yeager]] about her [[Parent|grandfather's]] occupation and how it had kept her [[Tamara Ryvora's family|family]] [[Foodstuff|fed]].

==Description==
A [[weapons factory]]<ref name="Interview" /> of the [[Galactic Empire]] operated during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="The New Trooper" />

==History==
{{Quote|You're just too young to understand, Tam. The Empire exploited the vulnerable that&mdash;''"<br />"''Oh, I understand. I understand that you're taking Kaz's side. Again.|Jarek Yeager and Tamara Ryvora, after the latter discussed her grandfather's past employment|audio=JarekTam-TheNewTrooper.flac|<ref name="The New Trooper" />}}
[[File:Imperial_Emblem.svg|thumb|left|200px|The factory produced weapons of war for the Galactic Empire (emblem pictured).]]
During the Empire's reign, the [[Tamara Ryvora's grandfather|grandfather]] of the [[human]] [[Technician|mechanic]] [[Tamara Ryvora]] searched for work and eventually began working for the [[factory]] to [[Foodstuff|feed]] his family after being unable to find employment elsewhere.<ref name="The New Trooper" /> At some point after he had stopped working there,<ref name="Interview" /> Ryvora was told of<ref name="The New Trooper" /> her<ref name="Minds Behind">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-resistance-final-season-interview|text=The Minds Behind ''Star Wars Resistance'' on What's Ahead in the Final Season}}</ref> grandfather's Imperial employment and how it had assisted her relatives,<ref name="The New Trooper" /> though was not informed the factory had been involved with making weapons of war.<ref name="Interview" />

While aboard the [[Trantor-class supertanker fuel depot|supertanker fuel depot]] ''[[Colossus]]''<ref name="The New Trooper" /> in [[34 ABY]],<ref name="Date">{{ResistanceDate|1|16}}</ref> Ryvora felt comforted by the protection offered by the [[First Order]]'s [[First Order stormtrooper|stormtroopers]], as the forces<ref name="The New Trooper" /> of the Empire's successor state<ref name="USWNE">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> reminded her of the way the Empire used to protect citizens<ref name="Minds Behind" /> during her grandfather's past. She briefly talked about her grandfather's former employment with her colleagues, the [[Resistance]] [[spy]] [[Kazuda Xiono]] and the mechanic [[Jarek Yeager]], who disagreed with her opinions on the First Order's practices and compared them to the Empire. However, Ryvora felt that her grandfather was an example of an Imperial employee with good intentions, which meant that the First Order's aims could also be beneficial. When Yeager began to reply pointing out the Empire's flaws, she scoffed and left.<ref name="The New Trooper" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Tam didn't really understand. [&hellip;] Her grandfather, her parents, you know, that were employed by the Empire wasn't a good thing, but she didn't quite understand it. She wasn't alive during that time.|Brandon Auman|audio=TamsFamily-BrandonAuman.flac|<ref name="Interview" />}}
[[File:StarWarsResistance-SeasonOne.jpg|thumb|right|190px|The factory was introduced via mention in ''Star Wars Resistance''{{'s}} first season.]]
The Imperial factory was first mentioned in "[[The New Trooper]],"<ref name="The New Trooper" /> the sixteenth episode of the [[Star Wars Resistance Season One|first season]] of the ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'' animated television series,<ref name="Insider 190">{{InsiderCite|190|Resistance Revisited|''Resistance'' Revisited}}</ref> which premiered on [[November 4]], [[2018]].<ref name="Disney Press">{{DisneyPress|wdtv=1|url=disneychannel/shows/star-wars-resistance/episodes|text=Star Wars Resistance}}</ref> ''Resistance'' executive producer [[Justin Ridge]]<ref name="The New Trooper" /> felt that having Ryvora discuss her grandfather's past<ref name="Minds Behind" /> as an Imperial factory worker<ref name="The New Trooper" /> on the show was important<ref name="Minds Behind" /> as it explained why she did not view the Empire as inherently evil.<ref name="Insider">{{InsiderCite|194|Switching Sides}}</ref>

Another of the show's executive producers, [[Brandon Auman]], revealed that Ryvora's grandfather's work for the Empire had taken place before she was [[Reproduction|born]]. The producer further indicated that Ryvora did not truly understand that the factory occupation that had provided for her family in the past was, in part, involved in producing weapons of war.<ref name="Interview" />

